WEBVTT

00:05:28.324 --> 00:05:31.494
on addressing this urgent global crisis?

00:05:32.328 --> 00:05:34.872
JF: Well, I think a lot of it
has to do with the fact

00:05:34.872 --> 00:05:39.335
that the fossil fuel industry
is embedded in our government.

00:05:39.377 --> 00:05:42.046
People on both sides
of the aisles are taking money,

00:05:42.088 --> 00:05:45.466
and so they don't speak out
against the fossil fuel industry.

00:05:45.508 --> 00:05:48.177
They only talk
about the green alternatives,

00:05:48.219 --> 00:05:49.637
and that's important.

00:05:49.637 --> 00:05:55.017
But not talking about fossil fuels
is like trying to bail out a sinking boat

00:05:55.059 --> 00:05:58.229
without plugging the hole, you know.

00:05:59.480 --> 00:06:04.276
But there's been progress because more
and more people do understand that,